physical.summary:
A carved wooden mask of female head with cloth and fibre hair attached and raised in an arch; the black fibre is stitched through the cloth densely resembling hair; the cloth is shaped at the back to hold the mask in position; through seventeen holes through the lower edge is fastened a fringe of knottede bundles of coarse brown fibre; a prominent grey mouth of two horizontal strips; white
groove between them; the nose large grey flared nostrils beneath a prominent oval; the eyes are deep upward pointing grooves beneath heavy projecting lids beneath a flat double arched grey band across the head representing eyebrows;
ears projecting white squares with grey central strip; grey scarification in ovals on cheeks and vertical strip in centre forehead; the main mask colour sandy yellow.

